The first and third lines are unchanged and must be reproduced exactly; only the middle line is new. Change nothing else in the file. Do not alter pwtLandedSha, the returned object, or the staged/not-landed branch below it.

PLACEMENT: the new statement goes AFTER the tap() call and immediately BEFORE the return. Performing this as a two-line replacement, with the tap line reproduced verbatim as the first line, is what guarantees the statement cannot be inserted into the wrong block.

WHY: this is the patch_with_tools escalation lane — the THIRD path that carries edit outcomes, after the EARLY and ROUTED feature_compose paths. Both of those received a recordDeterministicLabel call earlier today; this one was missed. recordDeterministicLabel drops any verdict that is neither marked deterministic nor prefixed 'deterministic:', and this path's reason begins 'landed <sha> —', so passing deterministic: true explicitly is what admits it — no change to the reason string is needed.

MEASURED: over a 4-hour live window, 50 edit-intent goals were detected, 14 reached a compose verdict, and 22 escalated to patch_with_tools. Roughly 44% of edit goals resolve in this lane, and patch-with-tools.ts contains zero references to recordDeterministicLabel or goal_verification_label, so none of those outcomes reach the oracle corpus in either direction. The edit-reach figure is therefore computed over a population missing this lane entirely.

All identifiers are in scope at that point: goal, pwtLandedSha. This is the LANDED branch, so reached is unconditionally true here and the staged branch below already grades honest-not-reached with its own hollow-template penalty; labelling this branch does not bias the corpus toward successes, it closes the half that was silent.

